Description: SSH2 for Python with legacy, INSECURE algorithms (paramiko_legacy)
 Paramiko 5 with the legacy SSH support that upstream removed in 4.0 and 5.0
 restored, for talking to old devices (switches, BMCs, embedded systems)
 whose SSH servers cannot be upgraded:
 .
  * DSA ("ssh-dss") host and user keys;
  * SHA-1 RSA signatures ("ssh-rsa");
  * SHA-1 key exchange: diffie-hellman-group1-sha1, diffie-hellman-group14-sha1
    and diffie-hellman-group-exchange-sha1, with 1024-bit group-exchange
    moduli;
  * GSSAPI authentication and key exchange.
 .
 These algorithms are broken or badly weakened. Modern algorithms are still
 preferred whenever the peer offers them.
 .
 The module is installed as "paramiko_legacy", so this package can be
 installed alongside python3-paramiko without affecting it: only code that
 explicitly does "import paramiko_legacy" gets the legacy algorithms.
